{"id":"word:hebrew:H3791","type":"word","title":"כָּתָב","subtitle":"H3791 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"something written , i.e. a writing , record or book","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to כָּתָב (H3791) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 16 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"כָּתָב (kâthâb) means something written , i.e. a writing , record or book First listed occurrence: 1Chr 28 19."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"כָּתָב","transliteration":"kâthâb","pronunciation":"kaw-thawb'","strong":"H3791","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3791","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["כִּ/כְתָבָ֔/הּ","הַ/כְּתָ֗ב","כְתָבָ֛/ם","בִּ/כְתָ֛ב","בִּ/כְתָ֔ב"],"morphs":[["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3fs",3],["HR/Ncmsa",2],["HR/Ncmsc",2],["HTd/Ncmsa",2],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",2],["HNcmsc",1],["HNcmsa",1],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3mp",1],["HC/R/Ncmsc",1],["HC/Ncmsc",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"something written , i.e. a writing , record or book","usage":"register, scripture, writing.","full":"H3791. kethab כְּתָב noun masculine Ezra 4:7 writing (late Aramaic; Biblical Aramaic כְּתָב Syriac ); — ׳כ absolute 1Chr 28:19 4 t.; construct Ezek 13:9 4 t.; suffix כְּתָבָהּ Est 1:22 2 t.; כְּתָבָם Ezra 2:62 3 t.; — writing: 1 register, enrolement , Ezek 13:9 ; Ezra 2:62 = Neh 7:64 . 2 = mode of writing, character, letter , ׳וּכ אֲרָמִית כָּתוּב הִנִּשְׁתְּוָן Ezra 4:7 and the writing of the letter was written in Aramaic (characters; so probably, see BeRy Ryle, compare Late Hebrew Hoffm ZAW i.(1881), 334 ff. ); compare Est 1:22 ; 3:12 ; 8:9 (twice in verse). 3 = letter , 2Chr 2:10 ; Est 9:27 . 4 of a royal enactment, edict 2Chr 35:4 (|| מִכְתָּב ), Est 3:14 ; 8:8 , 13 ; more fully כְּתָבהַֿדָּת 4:8 . 5 of a writing with divine authority 1Chr 28:19 ; ׳כ אֱמֶת Dan 10:21 , i.e. a book of truth.","rootNote":"from 3789 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver